(810, 227100, 'Topel Lee', 'topel-lee', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/rdSuihhgNggOA584YLWWSUDQI4G.jpg', 'Topel Lee is a Filipino film, television, and music-video director known for his distinct visual style and work in the horror and thriller genres. He began his career directing music videos for top local bands before moving into television and feature films. His notable works include Ouija (2007), Amorosa (2012), and Basement (2014). Lee is recognized for his cinematic storytelling, strong atmosphere, and visually striking compositions.', 'Topel Lee is a Filipino film, television, and music-video director known for his distinct visual style and work in the horror and thriller genres. He began his career directing music videos for top local bands before moving into television and feature films. His notable works include Ouija (2007), Amorosa (2012), and Basement (2014). Lee is recognized for his cinematic storytelling, strong atmosphere, and visually striking compositions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Directing', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'nm1760800', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:32:45', '2026-05-08 13:32:45', NULL),
(811, 1134885, 'Omar Chaparro', 'omar-chaparro', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/fAIDrbtyHBcDDbRdRZ3bvNesKU7.jpg', 'Omar Rafael Chaparro Alvídrez (Chihuahua, Chihuahua, Mexico; November 26, 1974), better known by his stage name Omar Chaparro, is a Mexican comedian, actor, comedian, singer, composer, producer, lecturer and radio and television host.\n\nHe is known for creating and performing his humorous characters in his radio and television programs where he is also a host, for acting in several Mexican and Mexican-American films and for his double starring role in Netflix\'s musical comedy film, in tribute to Pedro Infante, Como caído del cielo (Like Fallen from the Sky).\n\nIn addition to being mostly recognized in the Latin dubbing world as the Spanish voice of the panda \"Po\" in the movie Kung Fu Panda and its continuations.\n\nHe also established himself as a singer and has recorded two albums, among them, is his outstanding album entitled Me enamoré de ti, which included his three hits \"Sigues tan hermosa\", \"Me enamoré de ti\" and \"Aferrado\".', 'Omar Rafael Chaparro Alvídrez (Chihuahua, Chihuahua, Mexico; November 26, 1974), better known by his stage name Omar Chaparro, is a Mexican comedian, actor, comedian, singer, composer, producer, lecturer and radio and television host.\n\nHe is known for creating and performing his humorous characters in his radio and television programs where he is also a host, for acting in several Mexican and Mexican-American films and for his double starring role in Netflix\'s musical comedy film, in tribute to Pedro Infante, Como caído del cielo (Like Fallen from the Sky).\n\nIn addition to being mostly recognized in the Latin dubbing world as the Spanish voice of the panda \"Po\" in the movie Kung Fu Panda and its continuations.\n\nHe also established himself as a singer and has recorded two albums, among them, is his outstanding album entitled Me enamoré de ti, which included his three hits \"Sigues tan hermosa\", \"Me enamoré de ti\" and \"Aferrado\".', NULL, '1974-11-26', NULL, 'Mexico', 'Acting', 2, 'Chihuahua, Mexico', '[\"\\u0639\\u0645\\u0631 \\u0686\\u0627\\u067e\\u0627\\u0631\\u0648\"]', NULL, 'nm1410318', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:32:48', '2026-05-08 13:32:48', NULL),
