(817, 3247772, 'Lizeth Selene', 'lizeth-selene', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/o8BNtreaGlVJkSlsYjGtFzwkXpG.jpg', 'Lizeth Selene is an Acapulco, Mexico-based Mexican actress, singer, and musician. She gained to prominence after appearing fearlessly in the Netflix series \"Rebelde,\" which aired on the platform on January 5, 2022.', 'Lizeth Selene is an Acapulco, Mexico-based Mexican actress, singer, and musician. She gained to prominence after appearing fearlessly in the Netflix series \"Rebelde,\" which aired on the platform on January 5, 2022.', NULL, '1999-02-07', NULL, 'Mexico', 'Acting', 1, 'Acapulco, Guerrero, Mexico', '[\"Liz\"]', NULL, 'nm12597895', 'lizethselene', NULL, '2026-05-08 13:32:58', '2026-05-08 13:32:58', NULL),
(818, 18468, 'Gustavo Sánchez Parra', 'gustavo-sanchez-parra', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/ymg31PTbKfOxE7jV4QSgtCZKPbg.jpg', 'Gustavo Sánchez Parra studied at the most famous Dramatic Art school in Mexico, the Centro Universitario de Teatro. He landed his first role in Alejandro González Iñárritu\'s debut, Amores Perros, for which he was nominated for an Ariel for Best Supporting Actor.\n\nThen he worked in national and international productions such as Ridley Scott\'s The Fire of Vengeance; The Three Burials of Melquíades Estrada, by Tommy Lee Jones; Rabia, by Sebastián Cordero, and Crónicas, produced by Guillermo del Toro, among more than 35 films.\n\nHe was awarded the Honorary Prize at the Morelia Festival for having appeared in more than 40 short films.', 'Gustavo Sánchez Parra studied at the most famous Dramatic Art school in Mexico, the Centro Universitario de Teatro. He landed his first role in Alejandro González Iñárritu\'s debut, Amores Perros, for which he was nominated for an Ariel for Best Supporting Actor.\n\nThen he worked in national and international productions such as Ridley Scott\'s The Fire of Vengeance; The Three Burials of Melquíades Estrada, by Tommy Lee Jones; Rabia, by Sebastián Cordero, and Crónicas, produced by Guillermo del Toro, among more than 35 films.\n\nHe was awarded the Honorary Prize at the Morelia Festival for having appeared in more than 40 short films.', NULL, '1966-11-08', NULL, 'Mexico', 'Acting', 2, 'Mexico City, Mexico', '[\" Gustavo Sanchez-Parra\"]', NULL, 'nm0844761', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:33:00', '2026-05-08 13:33:00', NULL),
