(871, 11288, 'Robert Pattinson', 'robert-pattinson', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/3qZ09UE7lN6AtorfXFRYpEtSY93.jpg', 'Robert Douglas Thomas Pattinson (born May 13, 1986) is an English actor. Noted for his versatile roles in both big-budget and independent films, Pattinson has been ranked among the world\'s highest-paid actors. After starting to act in a London theatre club at age 15, Pattinson began his film career by playing Cedric Diggory in the fantasy film Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire (2005). He gained worldwide recognition for portraying Edward Cullen in The Twilight Saga film series (2008–2012), which grossed over $3.3 billion worldwide. After starring in the romantic dramas Remember Me (2010) and Water for Elephants (2011), Pattinson received critical acclaim for his performances in independent films from auteur directors. He starred in David Cronenberg\'s thriller Cosmopolis (2012), David Michôd\'s dystopian western The Rover (2014), James Gray\'s adventure drama The Lost City of Z (2016), the Safdie Brothers\' crime drama Good Time (2017), Claire Denis\' science-fiction drama High Life (2018), and Robert Eggers\' psychological horror film The Lighthouse (2019). He returned to mainstream films with a leading role in Christopher Nolan\'s spy film Tenet (2020), and starred as the DC Comics superhero Batman in Matt Reeves\' film The Batman (2022).', 'Robert Douglas Thomas Pattinson (born May 13, 1986) is an English actor. Noted for his versatile roles in both big-budget and independent films, Pattinson has been ranked among the world\'s highest-paid actors. After starting to act in a London theatre club at age 15, Pattinson began his film career by playing Cedric Diggory in the fantasy film Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire (2005). He gained worldwide recognition for portraying Edward Cullen in The Twilight Saga film series (2008–2012), which grossed over $3.3 billion worldwide. After starring in the romantic dramas Remember Me (2010) and Water for Elephants (2011), Pattinson received critical acclaim for his performances in independent films from auteur directors. He starred in David Cronenberg\'s thriller Cosmopolis (2012), David Michôd\'s dystopian western The Rover (2014), James Gray\'s adventure drama The Lost City of Z (2016), the Safdie Brothers\' crime drama Good Time (2017), Claire Denis\' science-fiction drama High Life (2018), and Robert Eggers\' psychological horror film The Lighthouse (2019). He returned to mainstream films with a leading role in Christopher Nolan\'s spy film Tenet (2020), and starred as the DC Comics superhero Batman in Matt Reeves\' film The Batman (2022).', NULL, '1986-05-13', NULL, 'UK', 'Acting', 2, 'Barnes, London, England, UK', '[\"R-Pattz\",\"Robert Douglas Thomas Pattinson\",\"RPatz\"]', NULL, 'nm1500155', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:34:46', '2026-05-08 13:34:46', NULL),
(872, 1639848, 'Mamoudou Athie', 'mamoudou-athie', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/ycUbhfZRKC8MtNK9oMwscRsl3uM.jpg', 'Mamoudou Athie (born July 25, 1988) is a Mauritanian-born American actor and producer. He is best known for his roles in the TV series Cake (2019) and films such as The Circle (2017), The Front Runner (2018), Unicorn Store (2017), UUncorked (2020), Kinds of Kindness (2024) and The Drama (2026). Athie was nominated for Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Actor in a Short Form Comedy or Drama Series for his performance in Cake.', 'Mamoudou Athie (born July 25, 1988) is a Mauritanian-born American actor and producer. He is best known for his roles in the TV series Cake (2019) and films such as The Circle (2017), The Front Runner (2018), Unicorn Store (2017), UUncorked (2020), Kinds of Kindness (2024) and The Drama (2026). Athie was nominated for Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Actor in a Short Form Comedy or Drama Series for his performance in Cake.', NULL, '1988-07-25', NULL, NULL, 'Acting', 2, 'Mauritania', '[\"\\u99ac\\u8499\\u675c\\u00b7\\u4e9e\\u63d0\"]', NULL, 'nm6974206', 'mamoudouathie', NULL, '2026-05-08 13:34:48', '2026-05-08 13:34:48', NULL),
(873, 1741367, 'Alana Haim', 'alana-haim', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/uOU4uueRxH5BYhzNjzPxJOxZStJ.jpg', 'Alana Mychal Haim (born December 15, 1991) is an American musician and actress. She is a member of the pop-rock band Haim, along with her two older sisters, Este and Danielle, where she performs piano, guitar, and vocals. In 2020, the band received a nomination for a Grammy Award for Album of the Year for their third album, Women in Music Pt. III.\n\nIn 2021, Alana starred in Paul Thomas Anderson\'s comedy-drama film Licorice Pizza, for which she received critical acclaim and was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Actress – Motion Picture Comedy or Musical and a BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Leading Role.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Alana Haim, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', 'Alana Mychal Haim (born December 15, 1991) is an American musician and actress. She is a member of the pop-rock band Haim, along with her two older sisters, Este and Danielle, where she performs piano, guitar, and vocals. In 2020, the band received a nomination for a Grammy Award for Album of the Year for their third album, Women in Music Pt. III.\n\nIn 2021, Alana starred in Paul Thomas Anderson\'s comedy-drama film Licorice Pizza, for which she received critical acclaim and was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Actress – Motion Picture Comedy or Musical and a BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Leading Role.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Alana Haim, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', NULL, '1991-12-15', NULL, 'USA', 'Acting', 1, 'Los Angeles, California, USA', '[\"Baby Haim\",\"Alana Mychal Haim\",\"Haim\"]', NULL, 'nm6076229', 'alanahaim', '', '2026-05-08 13:34:50', '2026-05-08 13:34:50', NULL),
(874, 2482808, 'Jordyn Curet', 'jordyn-curet', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/sUGk173dPdlR6OXQEape7EW2XT1.jpg', 'Jordyn Curet (born December 6, 2008) is an American actress known for her roles in The Drama (2026) and the Disney Channel show Raven\'s Home (2017-2023). She also made appearances in the show Bizaardvark and  the Academy Award-nominated film Marriage Story (2019).\n\nHer additional film credits include portraying a young Phylicia Rashad in The Tale of Two Sisters; voicing Livy in the animated film The Pit from Star Wars: Visions Volume 2; appearing as a human girl in Star Wars: Tales of the Empire; and starring in Project CC, Marvel\'s Black Widow, and the Disney+ reboot of Diary of a Wimpy Kid.', 'Jordyn Curet (born December 6, 2008) is an American actress known for her roles in The Drama (2026) and the Disney Channel show Raven\'s Home (2017-2023). She also made appearances in the show Bizaardvark and  the Academy Award-nominated film Marriage Story (2019).\n\nHer additional film credits include portraying a young Phylicia Rashad in The Tale of Two Sisters; voicing Livy in the animated film The Pit from Star Wars: Visions Volume 2; appearing as a human girl in Star Wars: Tales of the Empire; and starring in Project CC, Marvel\'s Black Widow, and the Disney+ reboot of Diary of a Wimpy Kid.', NULL, '2008-12-06', NULL, 'USA', 'Acting', 1, 'Campbell, California, USA', '[\"Jordyn Starr Curet\"]', NULL, 'nm4678576', 'jordyncuret_', 'jordyncuret', '2026-05-08 13:34:52', '2026-05-08 13:34:52', NULL),
(875, 1599899, 'Hailey Benton Gates', 'hailey-benton-gates', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/6gwH5IN15L4PXtLRwZYED6mO5xp.jpg', 'Hailey Benton Gates (born March 28, 1990) is an American model, actress and director. She is best known for her supporting roles in Marty Supreme (2025) and The Drama (2026). Her maternal grandmother is screenwriter Joan Tewkesbury, most known for writing the film Nashville (1975).', 'Hailey Benton Gates (born March 28, 1990) is an American model, actress and director. She is best known for her supporting roles in Marty Supreme (2025) and The Drama (2026). Her maternal grandmother is screenwriter Joan Tewkesbury, most known for writing the film Nashville (1975).', NULL, '1990-03-28', NULL, 'USA', 'Acting', 1, 'Los Angeles, California, USA', '[\"Hailey Gates\"]', 'https://vimeo.com/user42224820', 'nm3687486', 'haileybentongates', 'haileygates82', '2026-05-08 13:34:53', '2026-05-08 13:34:53', NULL),
(876, 71889, 'Michael Abbott Jr.', 'michael-abbott-jr', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/lL6epnepASAxQolqXeNve8hEcaR.jpg', 'Michael Abbott Jr. (born July 8, 1978) is an American actor. Abbott Jr. is an East Tennessee native and a graduate of The North Carolina School of the Arts Drama School. He has appeared in numerous stage productions in New York City and in productions across the country in some of the nations most prestigious regional theaters. He is also a proud member of John Houseman\'s Tony-honored, Acting Company. He made his feature film debut in writer and director Jeff Nichol\'s debut feature film Shotgun Stories in 2007.', 'Michael Abbott Jr. (born July 8, 1978) is an American actor. Abbott Jr. is an East Tennessee native and a graduate of The North Carolina School of the Arts Drama School. He has appeared in numerous stage productions in New York City and in productions across the country in some of the nations most prestigious regional theaters. He is also a proud member of John Houseman\'s Tony-honored, Acting Company. He made his feature film debut in writer and director Jeff Nichol\'s debut feature film Shotgun Stories in 2007.', NULL, '1978-07-08', NULL, 'USA', 'Acting', 2, 'Tennessee, USA', NULL, NULL, 'nm2534638', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:34:55', '2026-05-08 13:34:55', NULL),
(877, 1049916, 'Hannah Gross', 'hannah-gross', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/p94oyYrrywfSH3vkimTL1cbaWQt.jpg', 'Hannah Gross (born September 25, 1992) is a Canadian actress, known for her roles in Mindhunter (2017), Joker (2019), and Colewell (2019). Gross grew up in Toronto. She is the daughter of actors Martha Burns and Paul Gross. She attended New York University\'s Tisch School of the Arts and graduated with a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Theatre, minoring in Religious Studies.', 'Hannah Gross (born September 25, 1992) is a Canadian actress, known for her roles in Mindhunter (2017), Joker (2019), and Colewell (2019). Gross grew up in Toronto. She is the daughter of actors Martha Burns and Paul Gross. She attended New York University\'s Tisch School of the Arts and graduated with a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Theatre, minoring in Religious Studies.', NULL, '1992-09-25', NULL, 'Canada', 'Acting', 1, ' Toronto, Ontario, Canada', '[\"\\ud55c\\ub098 \\uadf8\\ub85c\\uc2a4\"]', 'https://www.documentaries.org/filmmakers/hannah-gross/', 'nm2193120', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:34:57', '2026-05-08 13:34:57', NULL),
(878, 1303156, 'Sydney Lemmon', 'sydney-lemmon', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/heGyUuth1HInFdywZ6y8gqjf0q6.jpg', 'Sydney Lemmon (born August 10, 1990; Los Angeles, California) is an American actress known for her roles in Fear the Walking Dead (2019), Succession (2019), Helstrom (2020), and on the theater stage. She studied BFA at Boston University (2012) and and earned an MFA from the Yale School of Drama (2017). Sydney Lemmon received a Julie Harris Scholarship. She also trained at the London Academy of Music and Dramatic Art.\n\nLemmon is the daughter of actor Chris Lemmon and granddaughter of Hollywood legend Jack Lemmon. She is also a singer and guitarist, writing music with her brother Jon Lemmon.', 'Sydney Lemmon (born August 10, 1990; Los Angeles, California) is an American actress known for her roles in Fear the Walking Dead (2019), Succession (2019), Helstrom (2020), and on the theater stage. She studied BFA at Boston University (2012) and and earned an MFA from the Yale School of Drama (2017). Sydney Lemmon received a Julie Harris Scholarship. She also trained at the London Academy of Music and Dramatic Art.\n\nLemmon is the daughter of actor Chris Lemmon and granddaughter of Hollywood legend Jack Lemmon. She is also a singer and guitarist, writing music with her brother Jon Lemmon.', NULL, '1990-08-10', NULL, 'USA', 'Acting', 1, 'Los Angeles, California, USA', NULL, NULL, 'nm5517526', 'sydney_lemmon', '', '2026-05-08 13:34:59', '2026-05-08 13:34:59', NULL),
(879, 209063, 'Zoë Winters', 'zoe-winters', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/3Ej5luqqvdD3hZXAzFZbdRxj7CQ.jpg', 'Zoë Winters (born February 20, 1985) is an American actress. She is most known for her recurring role on Succession (2018–2023), for which she won a Screen Actors Guild Award for Outstanding Performance by an Ensemble in a Drama Series. She has also appeared in Flatbush Misdemeanors (2022), Jules (2023) and Materialists (2025). She grew up in Santa Cruz, California and currently resides in New York City.', 'Zoë Winters (born February 20, 1985) is an American actress. She is most known for her recurring role on Succession (2018–2023), for which she won a Screen Actors Guild Award for Outstanding Performance by an Ensemble in a Drama Series. She has also appeared in Flatbush Misdemeanors (2022), Jules (2023) and Materialists (2025). She grew up in Santa Cruz, California and currently resides in New York City.', NULL, '1985-02-20', NULL, 'USA', 'Acting', 1, 'Santa Cruz, California, USA', '[\" Zoe Chasha Winters\",\"Zoe Winters\"]', 'https://www.zoewinters.com/', 'nm2925225', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:35:00', '2026-05-08 13:35:00', NULL),
