(1528, 1477143, 'Joseph Balderrama', 'joseph-balderrama', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/8BwRFsXzWD25dPih6IePcRD3EjT.jpg', 'Joseph Balderrama (born 1986) is a Mexican-British actor. His films include Stan & Ollie(2018). On television, he is known for his roles in the Netflix series Heartstopper (2022–present) and the BritBox series Hotel Portofino (2023). His voice work includes the video games It Takes Two (2021) and Diablo IV (2024).\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Joseph Balderrama, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', 'Joseph Balderrama (born 1986) is a Mexican-British actor. His films include Stan & Ollie(2018). On television, he is known for his roles in the Netflix series Heartstopper (2022–present) and the BritBox series Hotel Portofino (2023). His voice work includes the video games It Takes Two (2021) and Diablo IV (2024).\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Joseph Balderrama, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', NULL, '1986-01-01', NULL, 'Mexico', 'Acting', 2, 'Mexico City, Mexico', '[\"Pepe Balderrama\",\"Joe Balderrama\"]', NULL, 'nm1692732', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:50:02', '2026-05-08 13:50:02', NULL),
(1529, 58431, 'Abdul Salis', 'abdul-salis', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/2gDH3kNzUr4IUZLbCiYR9OCTjGa.jpg', 'Abdul Wahab Mumuni (born 6 July 1979), known professionally as Abdul Salis, is a British actor. He played paramedic Curtis Cooper on Casualty, the longest-running medical drama broadcast in the UK.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Abdul Salis, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', 'Abdul Wahab Mumuni (born 6 July 1979), known professionally as Abdul Salis, is a British actor. He played paramedic Curtis Cooper on Casualty, the longest-running medical drama broadcast in the UK.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Abdul Salis, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', NULL, '1979-07-06', NULL, NULL, 'Acting', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'nm1357414', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:50:04', '2026-05-08 13:50:04', NULL),
(1530, 216294, 'Lewis Hamilton', 'lewis-hamilton', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/8dqbTnI5y4k5plT4Kncp1PKeuHj.jpg', 'Sir Lewis Carl Davidson Hamilton (born 7 January 1985) is a British racing driver contracted to compete in Formula One for Ferrari. Hamilton has won a joint-record seven Formula One World Drivers\' Championship titles—tied with Michael Schumacher—and holds the records for most wins (105), pole positions (104), and podium finishes (202), among others.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Lewis Hamilton, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on', 'Sir Lewis Carl Davidson Hamilton (born 7 January 1985) is a British racing driver contracted to compete in Formula One for Ferrari. Hamilton has won a joint-record seven Formula One World Drivers\' Championship titles—tied with Michael Schumacher—and holds the records for most wins (105), pole positions (104), and podium finishes (202), among others.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Lewis Hamilton, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on', NULL, '1985-01-07', NULL, 'UK', 'Acting', 2, 'Stevenage, Hertfordshire, England, UK', '[\"Lewis Hamilton MBE\",\"Sir Lewis Carl Davidson Hamilton\",\"Sir Lewis Hamilton\",\"Lewis Carl Davidson Hamilton\",\"Sir Lewis Carl Davidson Hamilton MBE HonFREng\",\"Sir Lewis Carl Davidson Hamilton MBE\",\"Lewis Hamilton HonFREng\",\"\\u30eb\\u30a4\\u30b9\\u30fb\\u30ab\\u30fc\\u30eb\\u30fb\\u30c7\\u30d3\\u30c3\\u30c9\\u30bd\\u30f3\\u30fb\\u30cf\\u30df\\u30eb\\u30c8\\u30f3\"]', 'https://www.lewishamilton.com/', 'nm2619894', 'lewishamilton', 'lewishamilton', '2026-05-08 13:50:06', '2026-05-08 13:50:06', NULL),
(1531, 86270, 'Joseph Kosinski', 'joseph-kosinski', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/oWLUXWY0j8TYzwnf2wETYWO181S.jpg', 'Joseph Kosinski (born May 3, 1974) is an American film director. He directed the films Tron: Legacy (2010), Oblivion (2013), Only the Brave (2017), Top Gun: Maverick (2022), Spiderhead (2022), and F1 (2025). His previous work in computer graphics and computer-generated imagery (CGI) primarily involved CGI-related television commercials, including the \"Starry Night\" commercial for Halo 3 and the award-winning \"Mad World\" commercial for Gears of War.', 'Joseph Kosinski (born May 3, 1974) is an American film director. He directed the films Tron: Legacy (2010), Oblivion (2013), Only the Brave (2017), Top Gun: Maverick (2022), Spiderhead (2022), and F1 (2025). His previous work in computer graphics and computer-generated imagery (CGI) primarily involved CGI-related television commercials, including the \"Starry Night\" commercial for Halo 3 and the award-winning \"Mad World\" commercial for Gears of War.', NULL, '1974-05-03', NULL, 'USA', 'Directing', 2, 'Marshalltown, Iowa, USA', NULL, NULL, 'nm2676052', 'tacojoekosinski', 'JosephKosinski_', '2026-05-08 13:50:07', '2026-05-08 13:50:07', NULL),
(1532, 2446, 'Chad Oman', 'chad-oman', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/l84amvUZOrpSU5GRTDYoEkvbh25.jpg', 'Chad Oman (born May 15, 1965) is an American film producer and is the President of Production for Jerry Bruckheimer Films. Before joining Jerry Bruckheimer Films in 1995, he was a founding employee of the Motion Picture Corporation of America. \n\nHe attended the University of California at Los Angeles, where he studied screenwriting.  He then traveled to New York where he attended New York University, where he participated in the undergraduate film production program.', 'Chad Oman (born May 15, 1965) is an American film producer and is the President of Production for Jerry Bruckheimer Films. Before joining Jerry Bruckheimer Films in 1995, he was a founding employee of the Motion Picture Corporation of America. \n\nHe attended the University of California at Los Angeles, where he studied screenwriting.  He then traveled to New York where he attended New York University, where he participated in the undergraduate film production program.', NULL, '1965-05-15', NULL, 'USA', 'Production', 2, 'Wichita Falls, Texas, USA', NULL, NULL, 'nm0648288', 'coj3', 'OChad', '2026-05-08 13:50:09', '2026-05-08 13:50:09', NULL),
(1533, 15244, 'Ehren Kruger', 'ehren-kruger', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/jGwR9TRGhV9Fpw8cQrSN5FGQd9W.jpg', 'Ehren Kruger (born October 5, 1972) is an American film screenwriter and producer. He is best known for writing three of the five installments in the original Transformers film series: Revenge of the Fallen, Dark of the Moon, and Age of Extinction, in addition to the American version of The Ring and its sequel, The Ring Two and the American adaptation of Ghost in the Shell.\n\nFor his work on Top Gun: Maverick, Kruger was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ehren Kruger, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', 'Ehren Kruger (born October 5, 1972) is an American film screenwriter and producer. He is best known for writing three of the five installments in the original Transformers film series: Revenge of the Fallen, Dark of the Moon, and Age of Extinction, in addition to the American version of The Ring and its sequel, The Ring Two and the American adaptation of Ghost in the Shell.\n\nFor his work on Top Gun: Maverick, Kruger was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ehren Kruger, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', NULL, '1972-10-05', NULL, 'U.S.', 'Writing', 2, 'Alexandria, Virginia, U.S.', NULL, NULL, 'nm0472567', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:50:11', '2026-05-08 13:50:11', NULL),
(1534, 770, 'Jerry Bruckheimer', 'jerry-bruckheimer', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/sYjNrmbMi4DGAPX6Kt8wVy7LNXI.jpg', 'Jerome Leon Bruckheimer (born September 21, 1943) is an American film and television producer. He has been active in action, drama, comedy, fantasy, horror and science fiction. After working in advertising from college, Bruckheimer moved into film production in the 1970s. In the 1980s and 1990s, he partnered with fellow producer Don Simpson. Bruckheimer and Simpson\'s partnership continued until Simpson died in 1996. Bruckheimer has produced films including Flashdance, The Rock, Crimson Tide, Dangerous Minds, Con Air, Armageddon, Enemy of the State, Pearl Harbor, Black Hawk Down, as well as the Beverly Hills Cop, Top Gun, Bad Boys, Pirates of the Caribbean and National Treasure franchises. \n\nAt the helm of his self-titled production company, he has produced films distributed by numerous film studios such as Paramount Pictures, Sony Pictures and Disney. At the same time,  Warner Bros. Television and CBS Studios have co-produced his television works. In July 2003, Bruckheimer was honoured by Variety as the first in Hollywood history to produce the first and second-highest-grossing films of a single weekend: Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl and Bad Boys II. In 2023, Top Gun: Maverick earned him a nomination for Best Picture at the 95th Academy Awards.\n\nHis best-known television series are television dramas CSI: Crime Scene Investigation, CSI: Miami, CSI: NY, CSI: Cyber, Without a Trace, Cold Case, Lucifer and reality competition series The Amazing Race, which would spawn a franchise with international versions. For the latter, he won ten Primetime Emmy Awards. In 2003, three of his television productions—CSI: Crime Scene Investigation, Without a Trace and CSI: Miami—ranked among the top ten in the US ratings, making him the first producer to achieve this.\n\nBruckheimer is also the co-founder (with the late David Bonderman) and majority owner of the Seattle Kraken, the 2021 National Hockey League expansion team.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jerry Bruckheimer, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', 'Jerome Leon Bruckheimer (born September 21, 1943) is an American film and television producer. He has been active in action, drama, comedy, fantasy, horror and science fiction. After working in advertising from college, Bruckheimer moved into film production in the 1970s. In the 1980s and 1990s, he partnered with fellow producer Don Simpson. Bruckheimer and Simpson\'s partnership continued until Simpson died in 1996. Bruckheimer has produced films including Flashdance, The Rock, Crimson Tide, Dangerous Minds, Con Air, Armageddon, Enemy of the State, Pearl Harbor, Black Hawk Down, as well as the Beverly Hills Cop, Top Gun, Bad Boys, Pirates of the Caribbean and National Treasure franchises. \n\nAt the helm of his self-titled production company, he has produced films distributed by numerous film studios such as Paramount Pictures, Sony Pictures and Disney. At the same time,  Warner Bros. Television and CBS Studios have co-produced his television works. In July 2003, Bruckheimer was honoured by Variety as the first in Hollywood history to produce the first and second-highest-grossing films of a single weekend: Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl and Bad Boys II. In 2023, Top Gun: Maverick earned him a nomination for Best Picture at the 95th Academy Awards.\n\nHis best-known television series are television dramas CSI: Crime Scene Investigation, CSI: Miami, CSI: NY, CSI: Cyber, Without a Trace, Cold Case, Lucifer and reality competition series The Amazing Race, which would spawn a franchise with international versions. For the latter, he won ten Primetime Emmy Awards. In 2003, three of his television productions—CSI: Crime Scene Investigation, Without a Trace and CSI: Miami—ranked among the top ten in the US ratings, making him the first producer to achieve this.\n\nBruckheimer is also the co-founder (with the late David Bonderman) and majority owner of the Seattle Kraken, the 2021 National Hockey League expansion team.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jerry Bruckheimer, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', NULL, '1943-09-21', NULL, 'USA', 'Production', 2, 'Detroit, Michigan, USA', '[\" Jerome Leon Bruckheimer \"]', 'https://jbfilms.com/', 'nm0000988', NULL, 'bruckheimerjb', '2026-05-08 13:50:13', '2026-05-08 13:50:13', NULL),
(1535, 967387, 'Jeremy Kleiner', 'jeremy-kleiner', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/rRccbqvpL5HU73n1CLmJs9fyzzc.jpg', 'Jeremy Kleiner (born 1976/1977) is an American film producer. He and his fellow producers won two Academy Awards for Best Picture for the 2013 film 12 Years a Slave and the 2016 film Moonlight. Since 2013, he has served as the Co-President of Plan B Entertainment, serving with Dede Gardner.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jeremy Kleiner, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', 'Jeremy Kleiner (born 1976/1977) is an American film producer. He and his fellow producers won two Academy Awards for Best Picture for the 2013 film 12 Years a Slave and the 2016 film Moonlight. Since 2013, he has served as the Co-President of Plan B Entertainment, serving with Dede Gardner.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jeremy Kleiner, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', NULL, '1976-01-01', NULL, NULL, 'Production', 2, 'USA', NULL, NULL, 'nm1250070', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:50:14', '2026-05-08 13:50:14', NULL),
(1536, 20458, 'Dede Gardner', 'dede-gardner', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/uQ0Zgn4MZe5q1fMTb0m9Vi5ZqNK.jpg', 'Dorcas Wright \"Dede\" Gardner (born October 16, 1967) is an American film producer. She has been president since the founding of Plan B Entertainment and has been serving as Co-President with Jeremy Kleiner since 2013. She has won Oscars for producing the films 12 Years a Slave (2013) and Moonlight (2016), becoming the first woman to win two Oscars for Best Picture. She has also been nominated in the category for The Tree of Life (2011), Selma (2014), The Big Short (2015), Vice (2018), Women Talking (2022), and Nickel Boys (2024).\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Colson Whitehead, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', 'Dorcas Wright \"Dede\" Gardner (born October 16, 1967) is an American film producer. She has been president since the founding of Plan B Entertainment and has been serving as Co-President with Jeremy Kleiner since 2013. She has won Oscars for producing the films 12 Years a Slave (2013) and Moonlight (2016), becoming the first woman to win two Oscars for Best Picture. She has also been nominated in the category for The Tree of Life (2011), Selma (2014), The Big Short (2015), Vice (2018), Women Talking (2022), and Nickel Boys (2024).\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Colson Whitehead, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', NULL, '1967-10-16', NULL, 'USA', 'Production', 1, 'Chicago, Illinois, USA', NULL, NULL, 'nm0306890', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:50:17', '2026-05-08 13:50:17', NULL),
(1537, 2527414, 'Nicole Wallace', 'nicole-wallace', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/xlvq6OYCN6yQef4fpJQtwVyQxqr.jpg', 'Nicole Wallace del Barrio (born March 22, 2002) is a Spanish actress and singer, best known for her role as Nora Grace in Skam España and as Noah Morgan in the Prime Video original film My Fault.', 'Nicole Wallace del Barrio (born March 22, 2002) is a Spanish actress and singer, best known for her role as Nora Grace in Skam España and as Noah Morgan in the Prime Video original film My Fault.', NULL, '2002-03-22', NULL, 'Spain', 'Acting', 1, 'Madrid, Spain', '[\"Nicole Wallace del Barrio\"]', NULL, 'nm5913850', 'itsnicolewallace', NULL, '2026-05-08 13:50:20', '2026-05-08 13:50:20', NULL),
(1538, 2786960, 'Gabriel Guevara', 'gabriel-guevara', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/pviRYKEEmoPUfLYwP1VHJ6LQcRg.jpg', 'Gabriel Guevara (born February 6, 2001) is a Spanish actor, primarily known for his role as Nick Leister in Culpa Mía (2023) and Culpa Tuya (2024). He is also known for Charter (2020), Skam España (2018) and HIT (2020).', 'Gabriel Guevara (born February 6, 2001) is a Spanish actor, primarily known for his role as Nick Leister in Culpa Mía (2023) and Culpa Tuya (2024). He is also known for Charter (2020), Skam España (2018) and HIT (2020).', NULL, '2001-02-06', NULL, 'Spain', 'Acting', 2, 'Madrid, Spain', '[\"Gabriel Guevara Mourreau\"]', NULL, 'nm10140379', 'gabrieloxguevaraa', NULL, '2026-05-08 13:50:22', '2026-05-08 13:50:22', NULL),
(1539, 970027, 'Marta Hazas', 'marta-hazas', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/1dbeTFRCbWBt70dIGjYHKVLnpaG.jpg', 'Marta Hazas (born December 31, 1997)is a Spanish actress born in Santander (Cantabria). She has a degree in jorunalism, and she also studied dramatic arts in Cristina Rota School. She started her career with minor roles in Spanish tv shows like \'El comisario\', \'Hospital central\' or \'Los hombres de Paco\'. Fame came after her role as Amelia in the tv show \'El Internado\'. Before that, she played other leading roles in shows like \'Bandolera\' or \'Velvet\'. She also has been participated in movies like \'8 citas\' or \'Lo contrario al amor\'.', 'Marta Hazas (born December 31, 1997)is a Spanish actress born in Santander (Cantabria). She has a degree in jorunalism, and she also studied dramatic arts in Cristina Rota School. She started her career with minor roles in Spanish tv shows like \'El comisario\', \'Hospital central\' or \'Los hombres de Paco\'. Fame came after her role as Amelia in the tv show \'El Internado\'. Before that, she played other leading roles in shows like \'Bandolera\' or \'Velvet\'. She also has been participated in movies like \'8 citas\' or \'Lo contrario al amor\'.', NULL, '1977-12-31', NULL, 'Spain', 'Acting', 1, 'Santander, Cantabria, Spain', '[\"Marta Hazas Cuesta\",\"\\u0645\\u0627\\u0631\\u062a\\u0627 \\u0647\\u0627\\u0632\\u0627\\u0633\"]', 'https://martahazas.com/', 'nm1799971', 'martahazas', 'Martahazas', '2026-05-08 13:50:25', '2026-05-08 13:50:25', NULL),
