(1591, 2371545, 'Joel Kim Booster', 'joel-kim-booster', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/gKJHnWnnEoN85aC9UzAlg7XFnSG.jpg', 'Joel Alexander Kim Booster (born February 29, 1988) is an American actor, comedian, producer, and writer. He co-produced and wrote for Big Mouth and The Other Two and as an actor has appeared on Shrill, Search Party, and Sunnyside. In 2022, he wrote, produced, and starred in the Hulu romantic comedy Fire Island, a modern adaptation of Pride and Prejudice with a main cast of Asian American actors.', 'Joel Alexander Kim Booster (born February 29, 1988) is an American actor, comedian, producer, and writer. He co-produced and wrote for Big Mouth and The Other Two and as an actor has appeared on Shrill, Search Party, and Sunnyside. In 2022, he wrote, produced, and starred in the Hulu romantic comedy Fire Island, a modern adaptation of Pride and Prejudice with a main cast of Asian American actors.', NULL, '1988-02-29', NULL, 'South Korea', 'Acting', 2, 'Jeju, South Korea', '[\"\\u55ac\\u723e\\u00b7\\u91d1\\u00b7\\u5e03\\u65af\\u7279\",\"\\uc870\\uc5d8 \\ud0b4 \\ubd80\\uc2a4\\ud130\",\"\\uae40\\uc900\\ubbfc\"]', NULL, 'nm5527841', 'ihatejoelkim', 'ihatejoelkim', '2026-05-08 13:52:02', '2026-05-08 13:52:02', NULL),
(1592, 1700631, 'Liza Koshy', 'liza-koshy', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/pPu4TYkuNGmPEykWzFwCz55pAWB.jpg', 'Elizabeth Shaila Koshy (born March 31, 1996) is an American YouTuber, media personality and actress. Her main channel has amassed almost 17 million subscribers, and her two channels have over 3 billion views combined. She has received four Streamy Awards, four Teen Choice Awards, and a Kids\' Choice Award.\n\nKoshy began her career on Vine in 2013 before starting a YouTube channel. She made her acting debut as Aday Walker in Tyler Perry\'s horror comedy film Boo! A Madea Halloween (2016). She went on to star as Violet Adams in the horror drama series Freakish (2016–2017) and The Explorer in the YouTube Premium mystery series Escape the Night (2017–2019). She was also a correspondent for the MTV television series Total Request Live (2017–2018).\n\nKoshy co-created, produced and starred as the title character in the YouTube Premium comedy series Liza on Demand (2018–2021), which earned her several accolades, and hosted the Nickelodeon game show revival Double Dare(2018–2019), for which she received a Daytime Emmy Award nomination. She starred in the Netflix dance comedy film Work It (2020). She had voice roles in the animated adventure film My Little Pony: A New Generation (2021) and the science fiction film Transformers: Rise of the Beasts (2023).\n\nKoshy was included in the 2019 Forbes 30 Under 30 Hollywood & Entertainment list, the Time 2019 list of the 25 Most Influential People on the Internet and its 100 Next list that same year.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Liza Koshy, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', 'Elizabeth Shaila Koshy (born March 31, 1996) is an American YouTuber, media personality and actress. Her main channel has amassed almost 17 million subscribers, and her two channels have over 3 billion views combined. She has received four Streamy Awards, four Teen Choice Awards, and a Kids\' Choice Award.\n\nKoshy began her career on Vine in 2013 before starting a YouTube channel. She made her acting debut as Aday Walker in Tyler Perry\'s horror comedy film Boo! A Madea Halloween (2016). She went on to star as Violet Adams in the horror drama series Freakish (2016–2017) and The Explorer in the YouTube Premium mystery series Escape the Night (2017–2019). She was also a correspondent for the MTV television series Total Request Live (2017–2018).\n\nKoshy co-created, produced and starred as the title character in the YouTube Premium comedy series Liza on Demand (2018–2021), which earned her several accolades, and hosted the Nickelodeon game show revival Double Dare(2018–2019), for which she received a Daytime Emmy Award nomination. She starred in the Netflix dance comedy film Work It (2020). She had voice roles in the animated adventure film My Little Pony: A New Generation (2021) and the science fiction film Transformers: Rise of the Beasts (2023).\n\nKoshy was included in the 2019 Forbes 30 Under 30 Hollywood & Entertainment list, the Time 2019 list of the 25 Most Influential People on the Internet and its 100 Next list that same year.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Liza Koshy, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', NULL, '1996-03-31', NULL, 'USA', 'Acting', 1, 'Houston, Texas, USA', '[\"Elizabeth Shaila Koshy\"]', NULL, 'nm7862639', 'lizakoshy', 'lizakoshy', '2026-05-08 13:52:04', '2026-05-08 13:52:04', NULL),
(1593, 1453550, 'Chris Appelhans', 'chris-appelhans', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/33jtvCKnmBTb1pPMTobUMca7BkS.jpg', 'Chris Appelhans (born April 28, 1980) is an American illustrator, production designer, and director known for writing/directing Sony Pictures Animation\'s Wish Dragon (2021) and co-directing KPop Demon Hunters (2025). He started as a concept artist for films like Monster House, The Princess and the Frog, and Coraline, earning an Annie Award nomination for Coraline, and has illustrated children\'s books like A Greyhound, a Groundhog. He studied at Art Center College of Design and resides in Los Angeles with his wife, author Maurene Goo. Their son was born in 2020.', 'Chris Appelhans (born April 28, 1980) is an American illustrator, production designer, and director known for writing/directing Sony Pictures Animation\'s Wish Dragon (2021) and co-directing KPop Demon Hunters (2025). He started as a concept artist for films like Monster House, The Princess and the Frog, and Coraline, earning an Annie Award nomination for Coraline, and has illustrated children\'s books like A Greyhound, a Groundhog. He studied at Art Center College of Design and resides in Los Angeles with his wife, author Maurene Goo. Their son was born in 2020.', NULL, '1980-04-28', NULL, 'USA', 'Directing', 2, 'Firth, Idaho, USA', '[\"Christopher Appelhans\"]', 'https://www.sonypicturesanimation.com/our-team/filmmakers/chris-appelhans', 'nm2282774', NULL, 'dairysnake', '2026-05-08 13:52:05', '2026-05-08 13:52:05', NULL),
(1594, 3003169, 'Maggie Kang', 'maggie-kang', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/8OU7VfVMY7tfxUVFiBuy0zY9V3t.jpg', 'Maggie Kang (born June 10, 1981) is a Canadian film director. She created and co-directed KPop Demon Hunters (2025).', 'Maggie Kang (born June 10, 1981) is a Canadian film director. She created and co-directed KPop Demon Hunters (2025).', NULL, '1981-06-10', NULL, 'South Korea', 'Directing', 1, 'Seoul, South Korea', '[\"Maggie \\\"Min Ji\\\" Kang\"]', 'https://www.sonypicturesanimation.com/our-team/filmmakers/maggie-kang', 'nm3133422', 'nutmags', 'maggiemkang', '2026-05-08 13:52:07', '2026-05-08 13:52:07', NULL),
