(1654, 4474842, 'Peter Rice', 'peter-rice', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/eSsmBBf59xWmn1oAKfXtf3F1vz6.jpg', 'Peter Rice (born 1966) is a British producer and media executive. He is the former chairman of Disney General Entertainment Content for The Walt Disney Company and president of 21st Century Fox, where he worked from 1989-2019.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article, Peter Rice (executive), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', 'Peter Rice (born 1966) is a British producer and media executive. He is the former chairman of Disney General Entertainment Content for The Walt Disney Company and president of 21st Century Fox, where he worked from 1989-2019.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article, Peter Rice (executive), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.', NULL, '1966-01-01', NULL, NULL, 'Production', 2, 'UK', NULL, NULL, 'nm0723523', NULL, NULL, '2026-05-08 13:53:57', '2026-05-08 13:53:57', NULL),
(1655, 114019, 'Luke Evans', 'luke-evans', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/qUkYJcrDc4M0LHNYASs30luFvw0.jpg', 'Luke George Evans (born 15 April 1979) is a Welsh actor. Evans began his career on the stage, performing in many of London\'s West End productions such as Rent, Miss Saigon, and Piaf before making his film breakthrough in the Clash of the Titans 2010 remake. Following his debut, Evans was cast in such action and thriller films as Immortals (2011), The Raven (2012), and the re-imagined The Three Musketeers (2011).\n\nIn 2013, Evans starred as the main antagonist Owen Shaw in the blockbuster Fast & Furious 6, and also played Bard the Bowman in Peter Jackson\'s three-part adaptation of J. R. R. Tolkien\'s The Hobbit. Evans also portrayed the vampire Dracula in the character\'s film origin story, Dracula Untold. In 2017, Evans starred as Gaston in Disney\'s live action adaptation of Beauty and the Beast, and portrayed American psychologist William Moulton Marston, creator of fictional character Wonder Woman, in the biographical drama Professor Marston and the Wonder Women.\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia', 'Luke George Evans (born 15 April 1979) is a Welsh actor. Evans began his career on the stage, performing in many of London\'s West End productions such as Rent, Miss Saigon, and Piaf before making his film breakthrough in the Clash of the Titans 2010 remake. Following his debut, Evans was cast in such action and thriller films as Immortals (2011), The Raven (2012), and the re-imagined The Three Musketeers (2011).\n\nIn 2013, Evans starred as the main antagonist Owen Shaw in the blockbuster Fast & Furious 6, and also played Bard the Bowman in Peter Jackson\'s three-part adaptation of J. R. R. Tolkien\'s The Hobbit. Evans also portrayed the vampire Dracula in the character\'s film origin story, Dracula Untold. In 2017, Evans starred as Gaston in Disney\'s live action adaptation of Beauty and the Beast, and portrayed American psychologist William Moulton Marston, creator of fictional character Wonder Woman, in the biographical drama Professor Marston and the Wonder Women.\n\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia', NULL, '1979-04-15', NULL, 'UK', 'Acting', 2, 'Pontypool, Wales, UK', '[\"\\ub8e8\\ud06c \\uc5d0\\ubc18\\uc2a4\",\"Luke George Evans\",\"\\u039b\\u03bf\\u03c5\\u03ba \\u0388\\u03b2\\u03b1\\u03bd\\u03c2\",\"\\u0644\\u0648\\u06a9 \\u0627\\u06cc\\u0648\\u0627\\u0646\\u0632\"]', NULL, 'nm1812656', 'thereallukeevans', 'TheRealLukevans', '2026-05-08 13:54:00', '2026-05-08 13:54:00', NULL),
(1656, 2667928, 'Billie Boullet', 'billie-boullet', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/h632/2T18NEAVoU8cWWpAtaI6fTrdolX.jpg', 'Billie Boullet was born in London but moved to Paris as a baby, returning to the UK in 2014. She appeared in the Disney+ TV series A Small Light, where she played the role of Anne Frank, for which she was nominated for best supporting actress in a limited series by the Critics choice awards 2024. She also previously appeared in the CBBC series The Worst Witch. Billie is a fluent speaker of both French and Norwegian. She is set to star in Netflix’s Man on Fire, in 2026.', 'Billie Boullet was born in London but moved to Paris as a baby, returning to the UK in 2014. She appeared in the Disney+ TV series A Small Light, where she played the role of Anne Frank, for which she was nominated for best supporting actress in a limited series by the Critics choice awards 2024. She also previously appeared in the CBBC series The Worst Witch. Billie is a fluent speaker of both French and Norwegian. She is set to star in Netflix’s Man on Fire, in 2026.', NULL, '2005-04-05', NULL, 'UK', 'Acting', 1, 'Brent, Middlesex, UK', '[\"Billie Aimee Boullet\"]', NULL, 'nm11307049', 'billieboulletofficial', NULL, '2026-05-08 13:54:01', '2026-05-08 13:54:01', NULL),
